<title>RUSSIA: Russia plans equal gas pipeline access decree.</title>
<headline>Russia plans equal gas pipeline access decree.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian government will prepare a regulation on equal access to gas pipelines for all gas-producing companies, Interfax quoted First Deputy Prime Minister Boris Nemtsov as saying on Friday.</p>
<p>Currently all gas pipelines are owned by natural gas monopoly RAO Gazprom.  Giving other gas companies equal access is a key issue in restructuring Russian monopolies, which the recently reshuffled Russian government sees as one of its main goals.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
